error[type.list_element]: a list's elements share one type — the first is `A`, this is `B`
  ╭─[<case>/src/main.av:3:23]
3 │ let xs = [A { a: 1 }, B { b: 2 }]
  ·                       ┬
  ·                       ╰── this is `B`
──╯
help: to hold both, declare the list over a trait they share — `let xs: List<dyn Trait> = …`
